00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:50.040
>> Specifically what we did is we ran UGC

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:52.760
campaigns at scale and then turned those

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:55.040
creatives into paid ads. So essentially

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:57.320
how this works is you reach out to a

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:59.320
bunch of creators first and then filter

00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:01.240
them one by one by interviewing them to

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:02.800
see whether they have that virality

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:05.160
built in them. And typically we get a

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:07.040
10% conversion rate. So for every 100

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:09.480
creator we interview, we get actually

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:12.040
like nine to 10 good ones. Then you put

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:14.240
them on a monthly retainer plus a CPM

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:16.760
structure and then you test them. If

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:18.880
they're doing over 50,000 views per

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:21.320
video, then those are great videos that

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:24.080
you can run on Meta ads. So you can set

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:26.960
up test campaigns on Meta ads and then

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:29.120
figure out their ROAS on it. So if your

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:31.160
ROAS is greater than one, that means

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:32.919
you're making money from your app. And

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:35.240
Meta ads is not a linear growth

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:37.800
structure, meaning that if you're making

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:40.160
10% profit margin when you're spending

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:42.320
$100 a day on Meta ads, it does does

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:44.480
imply that if you spend 200 then you get

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:46.280
20% because there's diminishing marginal

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:48.600
return. So, you have to see whether your

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:50.880
ads are fatiguing or not on Meta Ads and

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:52.880
then basically pump out more creatives

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:54.760
so that you can test more options and to

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:56.640
figure out the most optimal creatives to

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:58.680
run on Meta Ads.

00:07:56.640 --> 00:08:01.160
>> I like that because yeah, working with

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:04.120
